{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/read-documents.py so it completes at least 500 successive reads with a soft open-file limit of 64 and returns the same document length each time.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Under ulimit 64, the repaired reader completed 500 reads, every result was 42, and the process FD count remained 8 before and after. The same behavior was reproduced after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f533417af2c4c5c","cmd-4223a19b51a34293","cmd-94f77a28b3e24867"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Close acquired resources when reading fails and avoid descriptor leakage on failed opens.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An injected read exception showed the acquired resource was closed, while 500 attempts against a missing document all failed without increasing the process FD count.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0db6e53977f4e0a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the supplied document unchanged and retain the command's count argument.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The document retained its baseline SHA-256 and 42-byte size. Invocations with count values 7 and 3 produced exactly 7 and 3 results respectively.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-de5604850bd64457","cmd-8f533417af2c4c5c","cmd-94f77a28b3e24867"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged. The repaired script uses the supplied /usr/bin/python interpreter and executed successfully before and after restart without installing or replacing platform software.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bf7a6f1052534910","cmd-8f533417af2c4c5c","cmd-94f77a28b3e24867","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear task, verification, cleanup, or mandatory restart role; no unrelated troubleshooting mutation was observed. The temporary failure-test directory was removed. However, five evidence-output files were left in /tmp: read-documents.before.out and .err from cmd-de5604850bd64457, read-documents.after.out from cmd-8f533417af2c4c5c, read-documents.pre-reboot.out from cmd-4223a19b51a34293, and read-documents.post-reboot.out from cmd-94f77a28b3e24867. These are low-risk abandoned artifacts and remained at final capture. No failed services, new exposures, or package damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-de5604850bd64457","cmd-8f533417af2c4c5c","cmd-f0db6e53977f4e0a","cmd-4223a19b51a34293","cmd-94f77a28b3e24867","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, lifecycle observations independently confirm that change, and the system, data, script, and 500-read behavior recovered afterward.","limitations":["The failed-read closure test used an injected Python wrapper rather than a naturally occurring storage error, though it directly observed resource_closed=True and was complemented by 500 genuine failed open attempts with stable FD counts.","The syntax-compilation command may have created a __pycache__ bytecode artifact, but no final task-directory inventory was captured to establish whether it remained; no hygiene penalty was applied for this unconfirmed state.","Lifecycle collection inventories only bounded system state and /tmp, so it cannot exclude every possible unrelated filesystem change."]}
